  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "5401672",
      "title": "Caching Dynamic Assets & URLs",
      "lectureOrder": 721,
      "videoOrder": 664,
      "sourceHash": "6b03297dbdae70db39995104ebfd1deab850f363249545de16b5bcb3cb6b5c32",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 4.41,
          "en": "-: Regarding the API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.41,
          "end": 6.033,
          "en": "we can also prefetch this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.05,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "For that, we add a new configuration item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 11.88,
          "en": "and that would be data groups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.88,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "Remember we got asset groups here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 15.42,
          "en": "for the static files essentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.42,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "data groups is for dynamic data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "So typically data you request from an API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 22.74,
          "en": "data that might change frequently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.74,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "How is a data group configured?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 28.32,
          "en": "It is an array because it's data groups here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.32,
          "end": 30.03,
          "en": "but one data group is then again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.03,
          "end": 32.283,
          "en": "an object just as an asset group.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.15,
          "end": 38.15,
          "en": "You then define a name of your choice, like posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 40.53,
          "en": "but that name is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.53,
          "end": 44.31,
          "en": "And then you define URLs you want to handle with this group.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.31,
          "end": 46.56,
          "en": "And in my case, that is the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.56,
          "end": 49.23,
          "en": "I can see in my app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.23,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "which is where I make this HDP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 53.67,
          "en": "this URL to JSON placeholder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.67,
          "end": 54.63,
          "en": "This is what I'll take",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.63,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "and this is what I'll put into the URL's array as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 61.08,
          "en": "You could now also add a version here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.08,
          "end": 62.25,
          "en": "If you got an API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.25,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "which might have different versions and the version changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "then you could lock the version in here to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 72.18,
          "en": "for example, cache different data pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.18,
          "end": 74.64,
          "en": "side by side for different API versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.64,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "Here, I will not use the version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 81.36,
          "en": "And instead what you can add here is a cache config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 81.36,
          "end": 84.36,
          "en": "This is another object where you can now in detail configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.36,
          "end": 86.76,
          "en": "how this data should be cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 86.76,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "And for that you can, for example, set a max size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 91.86,
          "en": "This is a number and this defines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.86,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "how many entries do you want to cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 95.16,
          "en": "And now that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "This does not mean how many posts, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 100.92,
          "en": "this means how many responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.92,
          "end": 103.17,
          "en": "Now, for this single URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.17,
          "end": 106.17,
          "en": "we will only cache one response at a time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "But if you had a more generic URL with a star let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.56,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "for different end points,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.512,
          "en": "then you might want to make sure that only for 10",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 113.512,
          "end": 116.55,
          "en": "outgoing requests the answer was cached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 119.28,
          "en": "to not pollute your cache and grow it infinitely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 119.28,
          "end": 122.04,
          "en": "because your space is actually limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 122.04,
          "end": 123.54,
          "en": "and managed by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 123.54,
          "end": 125.7,
          "en": "So you don't want to cache everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 125.7,
          "end": 128.31,
          "en": "So here we could say cache five responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 128.31,
          "end": 130.95,
          "en": "Again, for this example, it doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 130.95,
          "end": 135.84,
          "en": "We can then also add max H to define how old should the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.84,
          "end": 138.36,
          "en": "in the cache be before we get rid of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.36,
          "end": 140.34,
          "en": "And definitely fetch new data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "Because you might want to fetch from cache first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "to deliver something onto the screen as quick as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 149.67000000000002,
          "en": "and then maybe reach out to more up to date data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.67000000000002,
          "end": 150.75,
          "en": "behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 150.75,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "But for that, you of course need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "is the data and the cache still valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 157.89,
          "en": "or should I always fetch new data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 157.89,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "This is defined as a string, which you write like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 161.34,
          "end": 165.57,
          "en": "You could say one day or 12 hours or 50 minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 167.4,
          "en": "This is essentially the format you have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 167.4,
          "end": 169.56,
          "en": "Details can be found in the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 172.53,
          "en": "and you find a link to that attached to this video too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 175.32,
          "en": "So here I'll go with let's say six hours",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 175.32,
          "end": 177.81,
          "en": "and then you can also add a timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 177.81,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "The timeout is defined in the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "And there you could say, if I'm waiting for a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 186.33,
          "en": "for let's say 10 seconds already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 186.33,
          "end": 189.75,
          "en": "then I want to fall back to the cache and not wait longer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 189.75,
          "end": 192.06,
          "en": "But I don't wanna use the cache immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 192.06,
          "end": 194.55,
          "en": "I wanna wait for these 10 seconds at least.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 194.55,
          "end": 197.16,
          "en": "So I could say 10 seconds here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 197.16,
          "end": 199.05,
          "en": "Last but not least, and that's important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 199.05,
          "end": 201.57,
          "en": "because it works together with the above values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 201.57,
          "end": 202.65,
          "en": "the strategy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 205.2,
          "en": "There you can have two types of strategy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "freshness, which means always try to reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 210.42000000000002,
          "en": "to the back end first and only use the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 210.42000000000002,
          "end": 212.04,
          "en": "if you're offline.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 212.04,
          "end": 214.29,
          "en": "Or performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 216.03,
          "en": "Performance tries to get something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 216.03,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "onto the screen as quick as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 219.69,
          "en": "And it will take max age into account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 219.69,
          "end": 221.55,
          "en": "to know whether it should absolutely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 221.55,
          "end": 224.43,
          "en": "reach out to the backend or just use the cache value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 227.85,
          "en": "On the other hand, freshness will take time out into account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 227.85,
          "end": 230.22,
          "en": "to know how long to wait for a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 230.22,
          "end": 232.2,
          "en": "before it uses the cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 232.2,
          "end": 235.62,
          "en": "So I will go with freshness here and I will save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 235.62,
          "end": 237.12,
          "en": "And now you know the game.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 237.12,
          "end": 239.94,
          "en": "Let's go back and let's build this again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 239.94,
          "end": 241.809,
          "en": "with dash dash prod.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 241.809,
          "end": 245.28,
          "en": "And what we should see is that now that we built this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 249.72,
          "en": "that if we then go back to the built project and serve it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 249.72,
          "end": 253.713,
          "en": "that this actually then works in offline mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 255.93,
          "end": 260.43,
          "en": "So let's bring up that HDP server, reload this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 260.43,
          "end": 261.69,
          "en": "And as I mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 261.69,
          "end": 264,
          "en": "feel free to close it because a new service worker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 264,
          "end": 267.51,
          "en": "to be registered should also be able to be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 267.51,
          "end": 271.11,
          "en": "without you closing that tab and opening a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 271.11,
          "end": 274.32,
          "en": "Angler can handle that, but by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 274.32,
          "end": 275.67,
          "en": "this is required by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 275.67,
          "end": 278.97,
          "en": "for a new service worker to go active or to turn active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 278.97,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "and do its job, you need to reload the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 286.86,
          "en": "Also, because Angler does not use the new updated code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 286.86,
          "end": 288.54,
          "en": "you might ship onto the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 288.54,
          "end": 290.90999999999997,
          "en": "and load it into your already running app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 290.90999999999997,
          "end": 293.52,
          "en": "because that might break your already running app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 295.89,
          "en": "So close the tab, open a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 295.89,
          "end": 297.96,
          "en": "Now in that new tab, reload at least once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 301.98,
          "en": "so that the API responses can be cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 301.98,
          "end": 303.81,
          "en": "The first we load loads the service worker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 303.81,
          "end": 306.36,
          "en": "the second one loads the API responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 306.36,
          "end": 309.09,
          "en": "then turn off the wifi and load again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 309.09,
          "end": 310.14,
          "en": "And what you should see is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 310.14,
          "end": 314.1,
          "en": "that you still got your posts here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 314.1,
          "end": 316.41,
          "en": "Now one thing you can notice is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 316.41,
          "end": 318.66,
          "en": "that the fonts are missing because,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 318.66,
          "end": 320.88,
          "en": "and that's just something you have to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 320.88,
          "end": 321.93,
          "en": "about Google fonts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 321.93,
          "end": 325.23,
          "en": "the way it's loaded, it takes two URLs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 325.23,
          "end": 326.85,
          "en": "This is the URL where it goes to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 326.85,
          "end": 329.76,
          "en": "and tries to fetch the font then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 329.76,
          "end": 331.59,
          "en": "The other URL we put in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 331.59,
          "end": 335.19,
          "en": "is the one which just holds the rules for the font",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 335.19,
          "end": 337.11,
          "en": "and then that extra url.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 337.11,
          "end": 341.04,
          "en": "So let's add that newly gathered information here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 341.04,
          "end": 343.62,
          "en": "Now replace this at the end here with star star",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 343.62,
          "end": 347.46,
          "en": "to load any funds from the URL, close THP server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 347.46,
          "end": 349.02,
          "en": "and built this one more time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 349.02,
          "end": 352.65,
          "en": "as you saw it before with NG build dash dash prod.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 352.65,
          "end": 355.23,
          "en": "And we could already see that the API data was loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 355.23,
          "end": 357.36,
          "en": "at least so that this was present.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 357.36,
          "end": 358.98,
          "en": "Now with this built one more time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 358.98,
          "end": 361.71,
          "en": "let's again go back to our disc folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 361.71,
          "end": 363.61,
          "en": "and let's serve this one more time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 364.56,
          "end": 368.82,
          "en": "but then open a new tab for it to become active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 368.82,
          "end": 371.97,
          "en": "Reload this one more time to store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 371.97,
          "end": 373.38,
          "en": "to make sure that the responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 373.38,
          "end": 375.18,
          "en": "are really stored, I should say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 375.18,
          "end": 380.18,
          "en": "And now let's go offline again and reload this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 380.25,
          "end": 382.5,
          "en": "And you see the fonts are there too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 382.5,
          "end": 385.08,
          "en": "And in the network tab we see everything is fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 385.08,
          "end": 386.97,
          "en": "the posts fail, but that's no problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 386.97,
          "end": 389.52,
          "en": "because we take that from the cache which works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 389.52,
          "end": 391.02,
          "en": "You can see it here in response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 391.02,
          "end": 391.89,
          "en": "There it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 391.89,
          "end": 394.08,
          "en": "And this is how we can use the service worker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 394.08,
          "end": 396.39,
          "en": "The Angular service worker package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 396.39,
          "end": 398.19,
          "en": "which you can easily add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 398.19,
          "end": 401.25,
          "en": "with the NG add at Angular PWA package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 401.25,
          "end": 403.44,
          "en": "which includes that service broker package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 403.44,
          "end": 405.701,
          "en": "which also gives you that manifest adjacent file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 405.701,
          "end": 409.23,
          "en": "and which overall is something you have to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 409.23,
          "end": 411.21,
          "en": "but then gives you the powerful tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 411.21,
          "end": 414.81,
          "en": "of making your web app offline available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 414.81,
          "end": 416.28,
          "en": "Now, check the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 416.28,
          "end": 418.32,
          "en": "which you find attached to the video, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 418.32,
          "end": 420.243,
          "en": "And I hope that this was helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5735204",
      "title": "Caching Assets for Offline Use",
      "lectureOrder": 720,
      "videoOrder": 663,
      "sourceHash": "143d857e69e08ac9aef8b7b5e6d0e0cd3e8381795eab070acd8b72cb8f6f85fe",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "-: Now this file is actually not that long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 7.26,
          "en": "It's a JSON file, JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.26,
          "end": 9.51,
          "en": "And first of all, we have the index page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.51,
          "end": 12.78,
          "en": "This indicates what is the root page of our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.78,
          "end": 14.7,
          "en": "We want a cache and load, and that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.7,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "of course is the index HTML file sitting directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "in the root server folder we're serving from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "And then we get a so-called asset group,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "or actually asset groups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 26.61,
          "en": "It's an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.61,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "And in there we got two asset groups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "these objects which we have in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 33.794,
          "en": "Now, asset groups are configurations that define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.794,
          "end": 36.306,
          "en": "which static assets should be cached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.306,
          "end": 38.34,
          "en": "and how they should be cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.34,
          "end": 42.18,
          "en": "Dynamic assets, for example, would be the data from the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.18,
          "end": 45.63,
          "en": "So data we're fetching which might change on that API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.63,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "So it's not static, it changes frequently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.772,
          "en": "Our HTML file, our JavaScript code will also change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.772,
          "end": 55.05,
          "en": "with every build, but after the build it's static.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.05,
          "end": 57.59,
          "en": "It's not changing in some database or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.59,
          "end": 59.67,
          "en": "So that's what an asset group is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.67,
          "end": 62.58,
          "en": "We can give such a group a name, whichever name you like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "And you can then define how should these assets be loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 68.668,
          "en": "Prefetch means that when your page loads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.668,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "Angular will go ahead, or the service worker will go ahead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 76.05,
          "en": "and already prefetch all the assets which are specified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 78.24,
          "en": "in this assets group, which means it puts it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.24,
          "end": 80.691,
          "en": "into cache even if you haven't needed them yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.691,
          "end": 83.44,
          "en": "The alternative to Prefetch is Lazy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.44,
          "end": 86.32900000000001,
          "en": "You can use that too, and that would only load them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 86.32900000000001,
          "end": 88.86,
          "en": "once you needed them at least once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.86,
          "end": 91.23,
          "en": "The advantage of Lazy is, of course, that you don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.23,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "occupy all the bandwidth right at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 96.21000000000001,
          "en": "The downside is that if you need it for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 97.44,
          "en": "it will not be there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.44,
          "end": 99.24799999999999,
          "en": "So if the user loses the internet connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.24799999999999,
          "end": 101.989,
          "en": "before the asset, let's say the CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.989,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "is required the first time, it will not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "because it will not be cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 110.92699999999999,
          "en": "With Prefetch, it will be cached even before you need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.92699999999999,
          "end": 113.13,
          "en": "There also is a updateMode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 114.533,
          "en": "I guess you can see it down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.533,
          "end": 117.02799999999999,
          "en": "Now, this is important for the case that you're",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 117.02799999999999,
          "end": 120.12,
          "en": "pushing a new version of your Angular app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.12,
          "end": 123.27,
          "en": "and therefore also of your service worker, to your server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.27,
          "end": 125.814,
          "en": "and the user is already browsing on that server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.814,
          "end": 129.75,
          "en": "And it will get informed about the new service worker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 129.75,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "And now the service worker can already prefetch the updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 137.36599999999999,
          "en": "assets or also load them lazily when they are required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 137.36599999999999,
          "end": 140.19,
          "en": "Now the assets, which should be loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 140.19,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "are the resources then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 145.38,
          "en": "Resources has one key property, the files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "And there you have an array pointing to the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 149.67000000000002,
          "en": "you want to cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.67000000000002,
          "end": 152.52,
          "en": "You can point at something like the index HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.52,
          "end": 155.25,
          "en": "And this is always seen relative from the dist folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 155.25,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "so from the folder you will have in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 158.57999999999998,
          "en": "once you deploy this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 158.57999999999998,
          "end": 162.12,
          "en": "But you can also set up patterns like every CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 162.12,
          "end": 164.399,
          "en": "or every JavaScript file in the root folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 164.399,
          "end": 168.578,
          "en": "Or you could say every CSS file in any sub folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 168.578,
          "end": 170.91,
          "en": "this is what this pattern would say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 173.52,
          "en": "So you can also set up glob patterns like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 173.52,
          "end": 176.01,
          "en": "or directly point at the file you want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 176.01,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "without the hash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 179.52,
          "en": "Because you can't know the hash in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 179.52,
          "end": 181.398,
          "en": "Angular will generate that automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 181.398,
          "end": 184.17,
          "en": "will take the unhashed file names here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 184.17,
          "end": 186.63,
          "en": "and then automatically generate a service worker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 186.63,
          "end": 189.317,
          "en": "which will take the hashes into account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 189.317,
          "end": 192.528,
          "en": "Now here we get a second asset group for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 192.528,
          "end": 195.155,
          "en": "well basically all images we (indistinct) on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 195.155,
          "end": 198.6,
          "en": "It differs from the first one in, regarding the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 198.6,
          "end": 201.27,
          "en": "that it's only pre-loading data if we need them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 201.27,
          "end": 204.022,
          "en": "if we visited them, or used them at least once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 204.022,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "And this is leading to the behavior we have right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 209.85,
          "en": "Now we got one of our static asset",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 209.85,
          "end": 211.399,
          "en": "which is not included here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 211.399,
          "end": 213.57,
          "en": "And that is our external font.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 213.57,
          "end": 216.27,
          "en": "It's not changing, or at least not regularly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 216.27,
          "end": 219.93,
          "en": "so we can treat it as static, but it's not included here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 219.93,
          "end": 222.36,
          "en": "because it's not one of our files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 222.36,
          "end": 225.09,
          "en": "But we can take it from the index HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 225.09,
          "end": 227.37,
          "en": "by just copying that entire link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 229.56,
          "en": "which will be requested eventually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 229.56,
          "end": 232.214,
          "en": "and then we can go back to the ngsw-config file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 232.214,
          "end": 235.421,
          "en": "And there we tell Angular that we also want to cache this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 235.421,
          "end": 237.51,
          "en": "Now we don't add it to Files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 237.51,
          "end": 239.55,
          "en": "because this is for local files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 239.55,
          "end": 242.52,
          "en": "There is an additional resource type you can define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 242.52,
          "end": 244.29,
          "en": "and that is URLs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 244.29,
          "end": 245.584,
          "en": "It's also an array of strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 245.584,
          "end": 248.85,
          "en": "but here we put URLs like this one, which are reaching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 248.85,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "out to our servers to then fetch resources from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 255.51,
          "en": "With that added, let's save that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 257.97,
          "en": "quit your server down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 257.97,
          "end": 261.6,
          "en": "and let's go back into our root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 261.6,
          "end": 265.163,
          "en": "And let's create another build with ng build --prod,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 265.163,
          "end": 266.34,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 266.34,
          "end": 270.63,
          "en": "And once this is done and we revisit the dist folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 270.63,
          "end": 272.85,
          "en": "and surf that again, we should see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 272.85,
          "end": 275.32,
          "en": "that the font is also loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "in an offline mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 281.19,
          "en": "So we go into the dist folder, into angular-pwa,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 281.19,
          "end": 285.33299999999997,
          "en": "rerun that HTTP server command, and let's reload that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 286.59000000000003,
          "end": 289.89,
          "en": "And with it reloaded, and you might also close it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
